From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:06:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 114/151] "/" command menu in Markdown files

Typing "/" at the start of a line in a Markdown file opens a menu of
Markdown blocks: headings, lists, task list, quote, code block, table,
divider, link, image and Mermaid diagram, each with its syntax as a
hint. Typing filters the list (label words, English names, keywords).
Up/Down, Enter/Tab and Esc work the menu; the mouse highlights, clicks
and scrolls it. A pick replaces the "/query" with plain Markdown in one
undo step, with blank lines around blocks where needed and the file's
line ending.

The menu does not open in front matter, code blocks, HTML blocks or an
open HTML comment, in non-Markdown files or with Vim bindings. It is a
window overlay (new src/slash_popup.rs), so the editor's edges never
clip it; the logic lives in new src/slash_menu.rs, with tests.

Setting: Settings, Markdown, '"/" command menu' (markdown_slash_menu,
on by default).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

